    {
      "rank": 6,
      "row_id": 444413,
      "chunk_id": "5e41196bb358_1",
      "doc_id": "5e41196bb358",
      "text": "I don't think the iOS battery efficiency measurement is a good indicator for how well a battery will perform because lithium ion batteries have some inescapable memory quirks that'll create a false floor for total charge capacity if the battery is repeatedly charged before being completely discharged. Anyway... like I said, the quality of the phone in all other respects is great, not a single blemish. Just be aware that battery percentages aren't going to give you a full picture of how it actually performs. Update: 3 days later, the phone's battery health indicator has dropped from 92% to 85%. This is with just two complete discharges. Normally, that kind of drop would take a year. Either they're deliberately skewing the battery health results so they appear higher on arrival or there's a serious flaw in their process.",
      "score": 0.032690426839663694,
      "brand": "Apple",
      "model": "iPhone SE",
      "rating": 2,
      "timestamp": "2023-02-08",
